  <p class="rl-lede" style="margin-top:44px">These three are not rivals so much as layers: QP1's leaders and tabular figures live in tables and cards, QP2's spine belongs to page-level surfaces (article headers, tool mastheads, the Atlas), QP3's ticks and markers suit the map drawers. A doctrine can adopt all three WHERE EACH LIVES, and that is my recommendation. Verdict however you like: whole columns, single moves (leader dots yes, spine no), or the layered adoption. Then it all gets written into DESIGN.md as named rules and piloted on one surface.</p>
